Red Wine Shallot Jus
Serves: 6
Prep: 10 min
Cook: 30 min
Total: 40 min
Source: Serious Eats, Sasha Marx (from Tri-Tip With Shallot Jus)
Equipment: 3 l saucepan, Large skillet, Spatula

Finish (heat): Shallots into the reduction. Bring to a **simmer** over high heat and stir in the soy. Season.
  Reduce (heat, 15–20 min, then keep warm): Boil the stock and wine, then simmer, scraping down the sides, until reduced to **{475 ml}** and slightly thickened. Heat off.
    - 950 ml = 1 quart | Beef stock | or brown chicken stock
    - 240 ml = 1 cup | Red wine
  Deglaze (heat, ~1 min): Add the wine and scrape up the browned bits.
    Soften (heat, ~6 min): Oil, then shallots with a little salt and pepper. Stir often until **soft and lightly browned**.
      Slice: Peel and thinly slice.
        - 450 g = 1 lb | Shallots
      - 2 Tbsp | Vegetable oil
      - to taste | Salt & pepper
    - 60 ml = ¼ cup | Red wine
  - 1 Tbsp | Soy sauce
